    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25">

                <pb facs="0112" n="38" xml:id="pg38"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1639.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of Stat</hi>e, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>, </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-12-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 30, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I enclose herewith, for your information,
                    an anthenticated copy of an affidavit which was communicated to this department
                    by William Skiddy, esq., of Stamford, Connecticut, upon the subject of the
                    letter of Sir James Elphinstone to the London Standard. Mr. Skiddy participated
                    in the transaction referred to therein, and by his own statement destroyed the
                    applicability of the precedent to Waddell’s conduct.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>





